From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump fast-uri 3.1.7 -> 3.1.8 for CVE-2026-86472

Upstream: https://github.com/nicolo-ribaudo/fast-uri/commit/34bff8d3c2d57c73c41ef02c0e7a4b3e38c07c34

fast-uri folds a host to lowercase before percent-decoding it, so a
percent-encoded uppercase octet (e.g. %41) is never folded. For
scheme-relative references (//host) the host canonicalization path does
not run, so parse/normalize/equal disagree on the same host and a
case-sensitive allowlist/denylist can be bypassed. Fixed in 3.1.8.
Yarn cache regenerated and uploaded to lookaside.

